 "hooks": [
  "Nobody remembers who raised the {build} in the {biome}, only that {builder} was the last to keep its lights burning.",
  "The {build} appears on no map, though every trader knows the {biome} road passes it.",
  "Long before the village, {builder} built the {build} here and swore never to finish it.",
  "The {build} was a gift, or a warning; the {biome} has kept the answer.",
  "Three winters ago the {build} still had a roof. {builder} took it, plank by plank, and left the rest.",
  "Travellers say the {build} moves a few blocks every year, deeper into the {biome}.",
  "The {build} was the first thing {builder} built and the last place anyone saw them.",
  "Carved above the door of the {build}: one name, half scratched out.",
  "Every stone in the {build} came from somewhere else in the {biome}, hauled by hand.",
  "The {build} was meant to guard the {biome}. It guards only itself now.",
  "Once a week a lantern still burns in the {build}, though the {biome} road has been empty for years.",
  "The {build} was built in a single summer by {builder} and their two apprentices.",
  "Locals leave bread at the {build} and will not say why.",
  "The {build} sits exactly where the old river used to bend.",
  "A bell in the {build} rings when the weather turns, or so the {biome} folk claim.",
  "The {build} was abandoned mid-repair; the scaffolding is still up.",
  "Two families built the {build} together and have not spoken since.",
  "The {build} was here before the {biome} grew around it.",
  "Ask about the {build} in the tavern and someone will change the subject.",
  "The {build} marks the spot where {builder} turned back."
 ],
 "builders": [
  "a wandering mason",
  "an exiled cartographer",
  "a retired pillager captain",
  "a lighthouse keeper's daughter",
  "a monk who spoke only to bees",
  "a smuggler with an honest face",
  "the last of the salt merchants",
  "an alchemist who feared the dark",
  "a shepherd who counted stars",
  "a pair of stranded sailors",
  "a cleric who lost her faith",
  "a mapmaker paid in emeralds",
  "a blacksmith with one arm",
  "a witch who kept cats and secrets",
  "a drowned king's steward"
 ],
 "reasons": [
  "it was abandoned when the wells ran dry",
  "they left after a fire took the west wing",
  "a plague of phantoms drove everyone off",
  "the road was rerouted and the money followed it",
  "a feud over a single chest of loot ended it",
  "the ground shifted and the foundations cracked",
  "a raid emptied it in one night",
